      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I 𝙙𝙚𝙛𝙞𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙚𝙡𝙮 air on the side of it being best to have the Trust and Safety menu set standards 𝒊𝒕 𝒅𝒐𝒆𝒔𝒏'𝒕 𝒎𝒂𝒌𝒆 𝒆𝒙𝒄𝒆𝒑𝒕𝒊𝒐𝒏𝒔 𝒇𝒐𝒓.\n\nWe keep the Trust System's behavior absolute, static, and predictable this way. Besides; some users also may use the Trust system to disable shaders for performance. Cubed's shader is not a bad-performer, but if a user has chosen to disable shaders it's best to fulfil that setting.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
