      "value": "@{5a8410e2e35350152c0c8741|full_name}: Go cool off. If this conversation is making you angry you're probably a little too invested here.\n\n-\n\nA toggle that disables all shaders, that communicates it disables all shaders, should disable all shaders.\n\nIt's not complicated. \nA shader toggle is all we have right now.\nThe idea is to divide avatar features into categories, to group them up and adjust which are allowed by-rank.\n\nExceptions made would best be done through added features: a system for making exceptions. I'm not against that at all, in-fact I'm for it; but a better approach than one that undermines the intended behavior would have to be suggested.\n\nUncleanly taking a system meant to toggle and making it behave non-universally.. doesn't seem the right approach. Again, perhaps a system to permit and disallow shaders by-case could be suggested, that the user could work with.\n\nCubed's shader being dev-backed gives if credibility, and it would be one I'd be entirely on-board with being a default exception if there was a system to handle shader exceptions.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
